  "summary": "Strictly, the direct GNN-for-sepsis evidence is the set using message passing over relational graphs for early prediction of septic deterioration: [V0003] reports accuracy 0.74 on LedgerGuard; [V0002] reports F1 0.67 on AgriSat-4; [V0001] reports AUROC 0.60 on Atlas-ICU; and [V0004] reports MAE 0.81 on CellLife. These metrics are not directly comparable: accuracy, F1 and AUROC are higher-is-better discrimination scores, whereas MAE is an error score. I therefore rank the higher-is-better reports ahead of the MAE report, while noting dataset and metric heterogeneity. Because exactly five IDs were requested, [V0007] is included fifth only as the closest additional sepsis-prediction candidate; however, it uses self-attention encoder models on LedgerGuard with MAE 0.85, not graph message passing, so it is not direct evidence for graph neural networks.",
